For a **cone**, the radius $r$, perpendicular height $h$ and slant height $l$ satisfy $l^{2}=r^{2}+h^{2}$.

[tikz]% mathsmap-solid {"version":1,"kind":"analytic-cone","radius":2.1,"projectedRadius":0.672,"height":2.8}
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
% Orthographic cone model: base radius R, view elevation asin(b/R), projected apex height H.
% Rim (R cos(t), b sin(t)); silhouette tangencies satisfy sin(t)=b/H.
\def\rimRadius{2.1}
\def\rimDepth{0.672}
\def\apexHeight{2.8}
\pgfmathsetmacro{\tangentAngle}{asin(\rimDepth/\apexHeight)}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Ap) at (0,\apexHeight);
\coordinate (Rp) at (\rimRadius,0);
\coordinate (Lt) at ({-\rimRadius*cos(\tangentAngle)},{\rimDepth*sin(\tangentAngle)});
\coordinate (Rt) at ({\rimRadius*cos(\tangentAngle)},{\rimDepth*sin(\tangentAngle)});
\draw (Lt) arc[start angle={180-\tangentAngle},end angle={360+\tangentAngle},x radius=\rimRadius,y radius=\rimDepth];
\draw[dashed] (Rt) arc[start angle=\tangentAngle,end angle={180-\tangentAngle},x radius=\rimRadius,y radius=\rimDepth];
\draw (Ap) -- (Rt);
\path (Ap) -- (Rt) node[midway,right] {$l$};
\draw (Ap) -- (Lt);
\draw[dashed] (Ap) -- (O) node[midway,left] {$h$};
\draw (O) -- (Rp) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\coordinate (ra) at ($(O)!0.28cm!(Ap)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(O)!0.28cm!(Rp)$);
\draw (ra) -- ($(ra)+(rb)-(O)$) -- (rb);
\fill (O) circle (1.2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For a right **square pyramid** with base edge $s$, the face slant height, the perpendicular height and **half the base edge** form a right-angled triangle: $l^{2}=h^{2}+\left(\tfrac{s}{2}\right)^{2}$. The face slant height runs from the apex to the midpoint $M$ of the base edge. In a general right pyramid, the base leg is the perpendicular distance from the base centre to the relevant edge; it is not necessarily half that edge.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (-2.6,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.332,1.0);
\coordinate (D) at (-0.868,1.0);
\coordinate (O) at (0.866,0.5);
\coordinate (P) at (0.866,3.4);
\coordinate (M) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\path (A) -- (B) node[pos=0.25,below] {$s$};
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw[dashed] (C) -- (D) -- (A);
\foreach \U/\V in {A/B,B/C,C/D,D/A}{\coordinate (T) at ($(\U)!0.5!(\V)$);\draw ($(T)+(0,-0.09)$) -- ($(T)+(0,0.09)$);}
\draw (P) -- (A);
\draw (P) -- (B);
\draw (P) -- (C);
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (D);
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (O) node[midway,right] {$h$};
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (M);
\node[anchor=west] (baseLegLabel) at (1.55,0.25) {$s/2$};
\draw[thin,->] (baseLegLabel.west) -- ($(O)!0.5!(M)$);
\draw (P) -- (M) node[midway,left] {$l$};
\node[below] at (M) {$M$};
\node[above right] at (O) {$O$};
\node[below] at (0.866,-0.65) {Square base};
\fill (O) circle (1.2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
A right cone has base diameter $16\text{ cm}$ and perpendicular height $6\text{ cm}$. Find its slant height $l$.

The diagram shows half of its axial cross-section.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (R) at (3.2,0);\coordinate (P) at (0,2.4);
\draw (O)--(R)--(P)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\path (O)--(R) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\path (O)--(P) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (P)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$l$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Halve the diameter to find the radius: $r=16\div2=8\text{ cm}$. The slant height is the hypotenuse.

$\begin{align*}l^{2}&=6^{2}+8^{2}\\l^{2}&=100\\l&=10\text{ cm}\end{align*}$

Take the positive square root because $l$ is a length.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (R) at (3.2,0);\coordinate (P) at (0,2.4);
\draw (O)--(R)--(P)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\path (O)--(R) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (O)--(P) node[midway,left] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (P)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

