A right square pyramid has base edge $12\text{ cm}$ and perpendicular height $9\text{ cm}$. Find the face slant height $l$ in exact surd form.

The diagram shows the triangle joining the apex $P$, base centre $O$ and midpoint $M$ of a base edge. Here $s$ is the base edge length.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (M) at (2,0);\coordinate (P) at (0,3);
\draw (O)--(M)--(P)--cycle;
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\path (O)--(M) node[midway,below] {$s/2$};
\path (O)--(P) node[midway,left] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (P)--(M) node[midway,above right] {$l$};
\path (O) node[below left] {$O$};\path (M) node[below right] {$M$};\path (P) node[above] {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The distance from the base centre to the edge midpoint is half the base edge: $12\div2=6\text{ cm}$. The face slant height is the hypotenuse.

$\begin{align*}l^{2}&=9^{2}+6^{2}\\l^{2}&=117\\l&=\sqrt{117}\\l&=3\sqrt{13}\text{ cm}\end{align*}$

