workedExamples.solution_text:
Halve the face base: $18\div2=9\text{ cm}$. In either half-face triangle, the lateral edge is the hypotenuse and the face slant height is a shorter side.

$\begin{align*}l^{2}+9^{2}&=15^{2}\\l^{2}&=225-81\\l^{2}&=144\\l&=12\text{ cm}\end{align*}$

